alloc a, b, c, d: four new indices, each in its first life
    a 0:1  b 1:1  c 2:1  d 3:1
    generations  0:1  1:1  2:1  3:1
    free list    []
free b, then d: their generations go up now, before anyone reuses them
    generations  0:1  1:2  2:1  3:2
    free list    [1 3]
alloc e: alloc takes from the end of the free list, so index 3, in its next life
    e 3:2
    generations  0:1  1:2  2:1  3:2
    free list    [1]
the old handles
    d 3:1 is dead
    e 3:2 is alive
    b 1:1 is dead
    d and e share index 3 but not a generation, so d can never reach e
free d again
    refused: d is dead, nothing changes
    generations  0:1  1:2  2:1  3:2
    free list    [1]
alloc f, g: index 1 first, then a new one
    f 1:2  g 4:1
    generations  0:1  1:2  2:1  3:2  4:1
    free list    []
    c 2:1 was never freed: still alive
